-- Demo catalogue for product-service.
--
-- Twenty-five products across seven categories and eight brands, with prices,
-- ratings and stock levels that vary the way a real catalogue does: some items
-- discounted, some not; one out of stock and several below their reorder
-- threshold so the storefront's out-of-stock state and the admin dashboard's
-- low-stock tile both have something real to show.
--
-- Brand names are invented rather than borrowed, so nothing here implies a
-- relationship with a real manufacturer.
--
-- Product ids are deterministic (UUIDv5 derived from the SKU). inventory-service
-- and order-service seed the same ids in their own databases, which is how the
-- demo data lines up across seven separate schemas without any of them sharing
-- a table.
--
-- Imagery uses a keyword-based placeholder service. These are demonstration
-- photographs, not licensed product shots; image_url is an ordinary editable
-- field and an administrator can replace it from the admin dashboard.





